Chapter: ListOobNegative
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A negative index must trap. This is the other of the two list-index
 guards and it fails for a different reason from the past-end one: it
 compares against zero, not against the length, and it reads BEFORE the
 list rather than after it. Neither guard can stand in for the other, so
 each has its own file.

 `.fatal`: dies on UD2. The battery-visible half is
 codex/test/ops/list-index-bounds.codex.

Section: Entry

  read-before : List Integer -> Integer
  read-before (t) = list-at t (0 - 1)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("got=" & show (read-before [1, 2, 3]))
  end

